WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:01.640
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.940
The number is two one nine two.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:09.180
David p received a voicemail about reparations
for black Americans.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.510
Let's take a listen.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.420
Hi David.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:21.560
It's Mike calling and I was wondering, um,
well I watched the congressional hearing about

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:30.409
reparations and, um, it's very interesting
dialogue and I'm generally supportive of the

00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:39.130
idea of reparations, but I do think that the
conversation going on right now does have

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:45.510
the potential to backfire against the eventual
Democratic nominee and, uh, it has potential

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:54.249
to ignite the far right and it is just generally
unpopular with the wider American people,

00:00:54.249 --> 00:00:57.190
although I do think that we can make the argument
for it.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.780
So, uh, thank you.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.780
Yeah.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.659
Listen, I don't know about the popularity
of reparations for black Americans among the

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:06.560
broader American people have not seen polling
about that.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.560
Here's my view on it.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:13.420
I think that there is a very valid and completely
reasonable, uh, moral and philosophical debate

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.210
to be had about reparations for black Americans.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.170
How many generations after slavery does it
go?

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:23.810
How do you demonstrate that you are actually
descended from individuals that were slaves

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:28.020
in the United States rather than from families
that came to the United States after slavery

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.020
was abolished?

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.810
I'm totally up for having that discussion
in practice.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.250
Unless Democrats get a super majority in the
Senate.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.079
I don't see any way anyway that reparations
pass.

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:45.860
And thus I believe that in 2019 right now,
this is a distraction of a conversation and

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:54.300
I believe that it is not a pragmatically a
smart path for Democrats at large to go down.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.300
That's, that's my view.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:00.770
I don't see any way that you get a single
Republican, uh, when it comes down to voting

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.109
in the Senate, uh, or maybe more than three
or four Republicans.

00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:06.380
Uh, I don't, I just don't see any way forward
for this.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.160
And as a result, I don't think that it's particularly
smart politics to keep talking about this.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.650
Uh, at this point in time.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.020
If you disagree, I do want to hear from you.

